# Wave a Flag

## Objective
Use the help flag of a Linux binary to retrieve the flag.

## Solution

```bash
chmod +x warm
./warm -h
```

The program displayed the flag when executed with the `-h` option.

## What I Learned

- How to execute a Linux binary.
- Why `-h` and `--help` are useful.
- Always check a program's help before guessing its usage.

